WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.286 --> 00:00:19.908
When I reflect on the last eight years and the seventy cases in which I have been involved,

2
00:00:20.508 --> 00:00:24.130
none seem as sinister or as strange as that of the speckled band.

3
00:00:25.151 --> 00:00:30.438
Of course I cannot take the credit for solving the mystery; that claim belongs to my friend and

4
00:00:30.478 --> 00:00:32.700
associate, the famous detective Mr.

5
00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:33.580
Sherlock Holmes.

6
00:00:34.661 --> 00:00:40.746
It was during the early spring of 1883 when I awoke one morning to find Holmes standing over

7
00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:44.510
my bed in the apartment we shared at 221B Baker Street.

8
00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:47.532
"Watson, we have a new client!"

9
00:00:48.153 --> 00:00:48.633
he announced.

10
00:00:49.294 --> 00:00:52.056
"She is downstairs and seems to be quite upset.

11
00:00:53.017 --> 00:00:56.220
Get dressed and join us—oh, and bring your notebook.

12
00:00:56.936 --> 00:01:00.779
This looks as if it may be our most interesting case yet."

13
00:01:00.799 --> 00:01:05.902
"My dear fellow," I responded, "I would not miss it for anything."

14
00:01:06.863 --> 00:01:09.885
I quickly pulled on my trousers and buttoned up my shirt.

15
00:01:11.106 --> 00:01:16.930
In my haste I forgot to comb my hair, but I did remember to grab my favorite leather

16
00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:20.472
notebook. I hustled down the stairs to the sitting room.

17
00:01:21.353 --> 00:01:26.056
Standing close to the fireplace was a young woman of about thirty who appeared agitated.

18
00:01:26.816 --> 00:01:31.278
Her expression was tired and haggard, and a streak of gray ran through her hair.

19
00:01:31.298 --> 00:01:34.599
"Thanks for joining us, Watson," Holmes said.

20
00:01:34.619 --> 00:01:37.060
"This is Lady Helen Stoner.

21
00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:42.502
She arrived by carriage this morning to seek our assistance with an unusual situation."

22
00:01:42.522 --> 00:01:49.204
"Although I don't even know for sure," Miss Stoner added quickly, "whether a crime has been committed."

23
00:01:50.056 --> 00:01:51.717
"Well, if you would explain to Dr.

24
00:01:51.757 --> 00:01:57.060
Watson here what you have just told me, I believe we will all agree that there is, indeed,

25
00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:58.741
a mystery to be solved."

26
00:01:59.762 --> 00:02:03.604
"Of course," she began, with a slight tremble in her voice.

27
00:02:03.624 --> 00:02:06.425
"I am the stepdaughter of Dr.

28
00:02:06.465 --> 00:02:11.168
Grimesby Roylott, the last surviving heir to one of the oldest Saxon families in England.

29
00:02:12.148 --> 00:02:15.210
My mother was a young widow when she met the doctor in India.

30
00:02:16.091 --> 00:02:18.172
He had a successful medical practice there.

31
00:02:18.988 --> 00:02:25.010
Dr. Roylott agreed to marry her in exchange for her monthly pension—you see, my father was highly ranked

32
00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:27.911
in the military and left us with a hefty sum upon his death."

33
00:02:28.911 --> 00:02:31.952
At this Holmes gave a slight nod of understanding.

34
00:02:32.792 --> 00:02:34.493
Taking notice, Miss Stoner cut in.

35
00:02:34.513 --> 00:02:38.274
"Let me correct any misunderstanding if one exists, Mr.

36
00:02:38.314 --> 00:02:39.774
Holmes. Dr.

37
00:02:39.814 --> 00:02:43.535
Roylott was kind and caring to both my twin sister, Julia, and me.

38
00:02:44.195 --> 00:02:46.056
We were only two years old at the time.

39
00:02:46.956 --> 00:02:52.678
We lived together happily for the next few years until an incident forced us to return to England."

40
00:02:52.698 --> 00:02:56.119
"Would you explain this ‘incident,' Miss Stoner?"

41
00:02:56.799 --> 00:02:57.299
said Holmes.

42
00:02:57.319 --> 00:03:02.781
"My stepfather was a professional gentleman, but he did have a temper.

43
00:03:03.661 --> 00:03:08.863
When he discovered that one of our servants had been stealing food from the cupboards, he flew into

44
00:03:08.903 --> 00:03:10.723
a fit of rage and killed him on the spot.

45
00:03:11.563 --> 00:03:17.139
Fearing that he would be imprisoned, we fled the country and returned to his ancestral home near Waterloo."

46
00:03:17.159 --> 00:03:19.762
"The mansion called Stoke Moran?"

47
00:03:20.462 --> 00:03:21.303
Holmes inquired.

48
00:03:21.323 --> 00:03:25.046
"Yes, it has been in the family for generations.

49
00:03:25.907 --> 00:03:30.571
The mansion was not in good condition when we moved in, but we made it into a home.

50
00:03:31.512 --> 00:03:35.896
In fact, we were content for a long time until my mother died.

51
00:03:36.656 --> 00:03:40.720
She was killed in a railway accident eight years after our return."

52
00:03:41.668 --> 00:03:44.449
"I imagine this had a profound effect on your family?"

53
00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:45.790
Holmes asked.

54
00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:50.512
"It did," Miss Stoner responded, lowering her eyes to the floor.

55
00:03:51.552 --> 00:03:58.755
"Not only did we lose our mother, but upon her death, our kindhearted stepfather ceased to practice medicine

56
00:03:59.495 --> 00:04:02.357
and began to exhibit bizarre behavior.

57
00:04:03.537 --> 00:04:06.218
He locked himself in the house and rarely went out.

58
00:04:06.918 --> 00:04:10.360
When he did, he often ended up in heated arguments with the neighbors.

59
00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:12.161
It was terrible!

60
00:04:12.641 --> 00:04:17.423
He was even brought back to the house once by the police after he started a brawl in

61
00:04:17.463 --> 00:04:18.424
the nearby village.

62
00:04:19.224 --> 00:04:20.485
But that's not all, Mr.

63
00:04:20.505 --> 00:04:25.508
Holmes. Since he no longer worked, Stoke Moran began to decay even more.

64
00:04:26.568 --> 00:04:30.711
Julia and I attempted to keep the house up, but it was no use.

65
00:04:31.691 --> 00:04:34.253
What's worse, we could not keep any servants.

66
00:04:34.713 --> 00:04:39.095
They quit as soon as they saw the baboon and the cheetah—" "Baboon and cheetah?"

67
00:04:39.775 --> 00:04:40.496
I interjected.

68
00:04:41.256 --> 00:04:44.959
"Yes, my stepfather has a passion for exotic animals.

69
00:04:45.779 --> 00:04:49.942
He frequently imports them from India and allows them to run wild in the yard.

70
00:04:50.642 --> 00:04:51.323
It's awful!

71
00:04:51.863 --> 00:04:52.724
But that's not all.

72
00:04:53.684 --> 00:04:57.327
A few years ago, he invited Gypsies to live on our land.

73
00:04:58.087 --> 00:05:00.489
They have pitched their tents in the woods behind the house.

74
00:05:01.229 --> 00:05:06.953
The situation became so stressful that Julia's hair was already turning white before she died."

75
00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:12.440
"Your sister is dead then?"

76
00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:12.800
Holmes asked.

77
00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:15.361
I am always so impressed by Holmes' sensitivity in these delicate matters.

78
00:05:16.281 --> 00:05:19.922
Miss Stoner paused and put down the teacup she was holding.

79
00:05:20.843 --> 00:05:27.324
Then, after several moments, she said, "Julia died two years ago, and this is the mystery that I

80
00:05:27.464 --> 00:05:28.345
beg you to solve."

81
00:05:28.365 --> 00:05:31.685
"Watson, are you writing all of this down?"

82
00:05:32.486 --> 00:05:34.146
Holmes motioned to my leather notebook.

83
00:05:35.086 --> 00:05:38.047
I nodded and gestured to Miss Stoner to continue her story.

84
00:05:38.067 --> 00:05:40.828
"Julia was engaged to be married.

85
00:05:41.384 --> 00:05:44.747
She had informed us of her plans during a family dinner at Stoke Moran.

86
00:05:45.707 --> 00:05:50.151
Dr. Roylott was thrilled and insisted that the wedding be held in the local parish.

87
00:05:50.911 --> 00:05:52.793
But it was never to be.

88
00:05:53.433 --> 00:05:57.496
The night before the wedding, Julia came to my room just after midnight.

89
00:05:57.516 --> 00:06:01.860
‘Helen,' she said, ‘may I ask you a question?'

90
00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:04.261
‘Of course,' I replied.

91
00:06:04.281 --> 00:06:06.563
‘Do you hear whistling at night?'

92
00:06:07.083 --> 00:06:07.484
she said.

93
00:06:08.452 --> 00:06:11.293
I had had no similar experience and told her so.

94
00:06:11.313 --> 00:06:17.334
"She looked at me strangely and inquired, ‘Do you think it might be the Gypsies at the windows?'

95
00:06:18.335 --> 00:06:19.875
‘No,' I responded.

96
00:06:19.895 --> 00:06:22.536
‘If that were true, then I would hear it too.'

97
00:06:22.556 --> 00:06:25.777
‘Maybe it's the baboon or the cheetah then?'

98
00:06:25.797 --> 00:06:28.537
‘I don't think so,' I answered.

99
00:06:29.058 --> 00:06:31.298
But I had no other explanation to offer."

100
00:06:32.198 --> 00:06:37.560
Holmes leaned forward, a gesture I knew indicated that the young woman's story was of great interest to

101
00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:40.934
him. "Please he said, urging her on.

102
00:06:40.954 --> 00:06:45.318
"After our talk Julia excused herself and then went to bed.

103
00:06:46.098 --> 00:06:48.781
I did the same, but I was quite concerned for her.

104
00:06:50.102 --> 00:06:55.346
After tossing and turning for over an hour, I finally fell into a deep sleep until I was

105
00:06:55.406 --> 00:06:57.788
startled awake by the sound of Julia screaming.

106
00:06:58.729 --> 00:07:01.971
I burst out of bed and ran down the corridor toward her room.

107
00:07:02.892 --> 00:07:06.855
I heard the whistling sound and a clang of metal as a shiver of terror ran through my

108
00:07:06.896 --> 00:07:13.610
body. When I arrived at her door, I found it unlocked—we usually keep them locked for fear that

109
00:07:13.650 --> 00:07:15.730
an animal may wander into the house at night.

110
00:07:16.691 --> 00:07:20.352
Inside, my poor sister lay writhing in pain on the floor.

111
00:07:21.272 --> 00:07:25.833
I rushed to her side and held her in my arms, but nothing I did would ease her

112
00:07:25.873 --> 00:07:26.613
horrible pain.

113
00:07:27.614 --> 00:07:30.054
Then she said something that I will never forget.

114
00:07:30.075 --> 00:07:36.674
"She looked up into my eyes and, with considerable effort, gasped, ‘Oh my God, Helen!

115
00:07:37.014 --> 00:07:38.416
It was the speckled band!'

116
00:07:39.458 --> 00:07:44.144
I sent for medical aid, but my dear sister was dead."
